{#- WEBSITE › PHOTOS (mockup board 14, then Chase, 2026-09-27: "I'd like to be
   able to reposition the parallax zone itself"). Each photo frame on the site
   was four text boxes. Now it is the picture, with the WINDOW the frame shows
   drawn on it — drag the window to what matters, set the zoom to size it —
   and the frame as the site will show it.

   The faint lines above and below the window are how far it travels as the
   page scrolls (main.js, "whisper-parallax"). The window can go anywhere on
   the picture; lib/frame.js keeps the frame's edge hidden wherever it is.

   Replace goes through the same crop tool as every other picture here, and
   the new photo is in the frame with the rest of this screen's changes until
   Save. -#}

<p class="rolegate" id="phNotConfigured" hidden></p>

<div class="ph" id="phRoot" hidden>
  <div class="ph-thumbs" id="phThumbs" role="tablist" aria-label="Photos"></div>

  <div class="ph-work">
    <div class="ph-main">
      <div class="ph-pic" id="phPic">
        <img id="phImg" alt="">
        <div class="ph-travel" id="phTravel" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <button type="button" class="ph-window" id="phWin" aria-label="The part the frame shows"
                data-i18n-attr="aria-label:ph.window"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="ph-controls">
        <label class="ph-zoom">
          <span data-i18n="ph.zoom">Zoom</span>
          <input type="range" id="phZoom" min="100" max="160" step="1">
          <output id="phZoomOut" for="phZoom"></output>
        </label>
        <span class="c-gap"></span>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="phReplace" data-i18n="ph.replace">Replace photo</button>
        <input type="file" id="phFile" accept="image/*" hidden
               aria-label="Replace photo" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:ph.replace">
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="ph-preview">
      <figcaption data-i18n="ph.onSite">On the site</figcaption>
      {#- Drawn exactly as the site draws it: the same frame shape, the same
         object-position and transform-origin at the focus, and the same scale
         the site holds a photo at while the page is still (zoom × 1.12). -#}
      <div class="ph-frame"><img id="phPreview" alt=""></div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ms-savebar" id="phSaveBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="phDirtyCount"></span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="phDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="phSave" data-i18n="con.save">Save</button>
</div>
